given-names>HE</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Reversible unfolding of individual titin immunoglobulin domain</article-title><source>Science</source><year>1997</year><volume>276</volume><fpage>1109</fpage><lpage>1112</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9148804</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B28"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Saitoh</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Laemmli</surname><given-names>UK</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Metaphase chromosome structure: band arises from a differential folding path of the highly AT-rich scaffold</article-title><source>Cell</source><year>1994</year><volume>76</volume><fpage>609</fpage><lpage>622</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7510215</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B29"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Sedat</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Manuelidis</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A direct approach to the structure of eukaryote chromosomes</article-title><source>Cold Spring Harbor Symp Quant Biol</source><year>1978</year><volume>42</volume><fpage>331</fpage><lpage>350</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">98280</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B30"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Smythe</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Newport</surname><given-names>JW</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Systems for the study of nuclear assembly,  DNA replication, and nuclear breakdown in <italic>Xenopus laevis</italic>egg extracts</article-title><source>Methods Cell Biol</source><year>1991</year><volume>35</volume><fpage>449</fpage><lpage>468</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1664032</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B31"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Strunnikov</surname><given-names>AV</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>SMC proteins and chromosome structure</article-title><source>Trends Cell  Biol</source><year>1998</year><volume>8</volume><fpage>454</fpage><lpage>459</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9854313</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B32"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Tskhovrebova</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Trinik</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Sleep</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name><name><surname>Simmons</surname><given-names>RM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Elasticity and unfolding of single molecules of the giant muscle protein titin</article-title><source>Nature</source><year>1997</year><volume>387</volume><fpage>308</fpage><lpage>312</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9153398</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list><fn-group><fn><p>This research was supported by the Centre National de Recherche Scientifique.</p></fn></fn-group></back></article>